cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AI Safety Explorer, please cite the software as below. If you report results
  from it, also cite the exact version (a tagged release) you ran, and the corpus version and
  hash the Explorer records with every campaign.
title: "AI Safety Explorer: measuring how model behaviour changes as context framing becomes riskier"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Elliot
    family-names: Telford
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/etelford32/AI_Safety_Explorer"
version: 0.31.0
date-released: "2026-09-25"
abstract: >-
  A research instrument for one question: when context becomes riskier while the underlying
  reasoning task stays the same, how does a model's behaviour change? A versioned corpus of
  matched prompt twins that differ along one framing dimension, a reproducible runner, objective
  correctness against computed answer keys, register and expressed-agency readings with null
  controls, blinded human annotation, pre-registered analyses, and a live-session monitor for
  conversations with deployed models.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - evaluation
  - large language models
  - over-refusal
  - sandbagging
  - power-seeking
  - research instrument
